      "artist": "Connor Lee: WAvegetarian",
      "description": "A cenotaph erected to honor the \"colored citizens of Oberlin\" who died during or because of their participation in John Brown's raid on Harper's Ferry: John Copeland, Shields Green, &amp; Lewis Sheridan Leary. See John Brown’s raiders. Note that the death date of December 2 given for Green &amp; Copeland is wrong; it should be December 16. Shields Green's link to Oberlin is disputed; see Shields Green. Although located in a cemetery, none of the 3 bodies are buried there. The bodies of Green &amp; Copeland were used for anatomical dissections at the Winchester Medical College, &amp; the bones discarded. Leary's body was thrown in a packing box with other bodies of raiders killed, &amp; dumped in a pit; in C.E.1899 they were excavated (surreptitiously) &amp; reburied next to the bodies of John Brown &amp; Watson Brown, on his farm.",
