    {
      "filename": "Robert E. Lee's Demand for the Surrender of John Brown and his Party (at Harper's Ferry) - NARA - 300373.jpg",
      "title": "File:Robert E. Lee's Demand for the Surrender of John Brown and his Party (at Harper's Ferry) - NARA - 300373.jpg",
      "url": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/5/52/Robert_E._Lee%27s_Demand_for_the_Surrender_of_John_Brown_and_his_Party_%28at_Harper%27s_Ferry%29_-_NARA_-_300373.jpg",
      "descriptionUrl": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Robert_E._Lee%27s_Demand_for_the_Surrender_of_John_Brown_and_his_Party_(at_Harper%27s_Ferry)_-_NARA_-_300373.jpg",
      "width": 2415,
      "height": 3000,
      "mime": "image/jpeg",
      "license": "Public domain",
      "artist": "Unknown authorUnknown author or not provided",
      "description": "Scope and content:  The destruction of slavery in the United States was the driving ambition of abolitionist John Brown. He came to believe that it would take bloodshed to root out the evil of slavery, and by the mid-1850's he dedicated himself to an all-out war for slave liberation. On October 16, 1859, he and his \"army\" of some 20 men seized the federal arsenal at Harper's Ferry, Virginia (now West Virginia). By the morning of October 18, Marines under the command of Bvt. Col. Robert E. Lee, stormed the building and captured Brown and the survivors of his party. When Brown refused to unconditionally accept the terms of this note, Lee gave this order to storm the building.\nGeneral notes:  Letters Received, Main Series, File W-386, Box 857. Exhibit History: \"American Originals,\" December 1996 - December 1997, National Archives Rotunda, Washington, DC, 624.0052.",
      "dateCreated": "18 October 1859<div style=\"display: none;\">date QS:P571,+1859-10-18T00:00:00Z/11</div>",
      "categories": [
        "1859 letters",
        "Artworks without Wikidata item",
        "CC-PD-Mark",
        "Documents related to Robert Edward Lee",
